Z||000007||Joe4x4||02-13-2001||06:02 PM||||No 87-Vette.....I was gonnna bid on it at last 10 min but I waited to long it was over ! <P> I had a 84 , 86 , 87 .....87 was a little better than the first year of the C-4. (84)<P>The winning bid was $8,000 .<BR>That is a good but for a 87 with greenwood <BR>and extra goodies it had .<P>I`ll just have to wait for the next deal <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||02-13-2001||07:13 PM||||We have a 87 with 18,000 miles on it. The car is hard to get in and out of, But the technology is amazing for the time , it pulls 0 to 60 in 5.6 sec STOCK runs low 14's , C4 vettes are probably the best performance value there is. But there not for everyone. In all the years we have owned and autocrossed the car it has onl;y worn out tires , an alternator and a brake booster. This is hard Hard driving..<P><BR>Fun cars ...Loads of torque. Get a mid 86 or later. some 86's have iron heads , later 86's have aluminum , all 86 converts have aluminum heads. Also you may want to look into a CAGS for it , it disables the skip shift on 2nd and 3rd gear , but leaves the OD in 4th , available from ecklers it's around $50 , just plugs in , in about 10 min<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||02-14-2001||02:32 PM||||My dad has an 82. I love the looks and the power, but I like driving my Fiero over that any day. I feel too confined in the vet. It has a different seating position and your a lot closer to the door panel. I feel wedged and I am 6 ft. 175 lbs. I'd hate to be big and fit in a vet.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||02-16-2001||01:34 AM||||The last Vette I owned was an '82 CE.  I bought it for the looks (drool), but power???  The last of the C3s were the most anemic of the modern Vettes.  Something like 180 hp.  You can get that much out of a Fiero (while weighing more than 1000# less).    ||||reg||1
Z||000011||hugh||02-16-2001||07:13 AM||||I had a 74 with the 454 engine(270HP).I changed the cam,had the heads done,put on a tri-power setup.It had a custom front end and hood.Nice car,great sound from the 4" exhaust.It was easier to use my wife's car,which was also more comfortable.I got about 8 miles per gallon.My GN would blow it's doors off and gets over 20 MPG on the highway and about 15 around town. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||2xsess||02-16-2001||10:29 AM||||My dad has an 88 Vette, automatic, I like driving it, the digital dash is awesome. It has 140,000 miles on it and the handling is still tight as he!!. It has decent power. I like the C-3s and the C-4s are ok.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
